lib/API/Docker/API/Images.pm:410: $params{tag} = $opts{tag} // 'latest' is sent whenever the caller gave none, so pull(fromImage => 'nginx:1.25') goes out as ?fromImage=nginx:1.25&tag=latest. spec /images/create: 'If both fromImage and tag are provided, tag takes precedence' -- moby replaces the tag (pulls nginx:latest, reports success); Podman concatenates to nginx:1.25:latest and answers 500 'invalid reference format'. Same for a digest reference (alpine@sha256:... becomes ...:latest). Not measured live (a pull mutates); measurable with a name that resolves nowhere, e.g. POST /images/create?fromImage=localhost:1/nope:1.0&tag=latest. Fix shape: default tag only when fromImage carries neither a :tag after the last / nor an @digest. t/images.t:205 mocks POST /images/create without asserting the query -- add that assertion (api-docker-test-writer) with the fix (api-docker-engine-worker). Found in the 0.004 pre-release grill.
